__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
venv/
.git

# --- Added 2026-08-16 (SESSION_20260812_FINDINGS.md finding 10) ---
# Dockerfile:11 is `COPY . .`, so anything not excluded here is baked into
# every image layer. Two problems that fixes:
#   1. Size. database/ was 810MB — trades.db (305MB) plus two backups
#      (504MB) — copied into every build and duplicated across cached
#      layer sets. logs/ adds frozen copies of the live host logs.
#   2. Correctness. At runtime docker-compose mounts ./database over
#      /app/database, so the baked copy is invisible — until the mount
#      fails or is misconfigured, at which point the container would
#      silently run against a build-time DB snapshot instead of failing.
#      Same class for logs/: reading /app/logs/watchdog.log inside the
#      container used to return ~3-week-stale data that looked live.
#
# NOTE the granularity: exclude the DATA files, NOT the database/
# directory. database/ is also the Python package (__init__.py, db.py,
# models.py) — excluding it wholesale would strip those from the image and
# leave the container importable only by grace of the bind mount.
database/*.db
database/*.db-shm
database/*.db-wal
database/*.bak-*

# Container-local and recreated by Dockerfile's `mkdir -p /app/logs`.
# Nothing reads these at build time; runtime writes recreate what it needs.
logs/
